<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="recommended-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/spell_holy_holybolt.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Recommended Gear for Holy Paladins in Mists of Pandaria Classic</span></h2>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="what-is-the-bis-holy-paladin-gear">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_questionmark.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> What is the BiS Holy Paladin gear?</h3>With many different sources of gearing and loot scarcity in Mists of Pandaria Classic, targeting your absolute Best in Slot gear isn't entirely realistic; instead, we've created a Best in Slot list from the ideal Holy Paladin drops found in Phase 3 from raids, dungeons, Reputation, and World Bosses to help you decide what to prioritize.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>While raid drops are generally the most reliable way of getting high item level gear, many other items can be just as good, if not better, so you should reference the <a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/guide/classes/paladin/holy/healer-stat-priority-pve">Stat Priorities for Holy Paladins guide</a> to help determine your own BiS gear based on what is available to you.<ul class="exclude-units"></ul>
<br/>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="bis-gear">Overall Best in Slot Gear for Holy Paladin</h3>Unlike the previous phases, BiS gear in Phase 3 is sourced exclusively from the new <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6622/throne-of-thunder">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Throne of Thunder</span></a> raid. A large raid with many bosses, and thus many loot options, the situation in Phase 3 is further complicated by the addition of Thunderforging, a mechanic which allows for most items to have a chance of dropping at a higher level than would be normal in Normal or Heroic raids. New to Mists of Pandaria Classic however is that standard (ie non-Thunderforged) Throne of Thunder drops can be upgraded to be equivalent to Thuderforged pieces. As such, both fully upgraded gear or their Thunderforged equivalents should be considered as identical, and either version perfectly replaces the other in the BiS list below.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<div class="clear exclude-units"></div>
