<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="set-bonuses">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_treasurechest02b.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Tier &amp; Set Bonuses for Holy Paladins in Mists of Pandaria Classic</span></h2>
<a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6622/throne-of-thunder">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Throne of Thunder</span></a> brings with it the Tier 15 sets, which for Holy Paladin is a strong upgrade over the Tier 14 set <a data-entity="item-set" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item-set=1134/white-tiger-vestments">
<span class="tinyicontxt">White Tiger Vestments</span></a>. While this transition does mean losing out on the <a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=123102/item-paladin-t14-holy-2p-bonus">10% reduced mana cost of Holy Radiance</a> of the previous set, mana at this point in the expansion is generally not of major concern due to overall iLvl increases, (particularly when it is possible to melee occasionally), and the boost to tank healing via increased <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=53563/beacon-of-light">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_beaconoflight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Beacon of Light</span></a> transfer is particularly welcome. There is generally speaking no playstyle difference involved when equipping Tier 15 as it is entirely a throughput upgrade for both the 2 and 4 set bonuses,  though players may find a slight timing adjustment to be had with their rotation given they will be effectively adding a second to the cooldown of <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=81453/holy-shock">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_searinglight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Holy Shock</span></a> from losing the previous <a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=123103/item-paladin-t14-holy-4p-bonus">4-set bonus</a>. As was the case with the Tier 14 set, the <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=114163/eternal-flame">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_torch_thrown.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Eternal Flame</span></a> playstyle gains relatively more power from Tier 15 than does <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=85804/selfless-healer">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_gaurdedbythelight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Selfless Healer</span></a>, but it is still powerful for both and there is no reason to overlook equipping it for non-tier pieces.<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="tier-15">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">Tier 15 - <a data-entity="item-set" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item-set=1163/vestments-of-the-lightning-emperor">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Vestments of the Lightning Emperor</span></a></span></h3>
