<br/>
<br/>Generally speaking those who possess Heroic Tier 14 should not replace these items with the Celestial version of Tier 15, though picking up pieces of this lower iLvl version may still be beneficial as Normal Tier 15 does quickly outpace the Heroic version of the previous set, and being able to activate the new 4-set as soon as possible is ideal. There is little if any reason to run both 2-set bonuses in tandem.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_inscription_trinket_crane.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Holy Paladins Trinkets in Phase 3</span></h2>In general, Holy Paladin's trinkets for should be centered around mana-regen, particularly prior to full BiS. That said, modern changes in Mists of Pandaria Classic have made Holy Paladin's slightly less mana hungry than is traditional,  and players in strong guilds may find that they quickly grow out of mana concerns and can find room for output trinkets.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>You should typically use one on-use and one passive trinket, or two passive trinkets, but rarely ever two on-use. The various options are listed below in order of relative strength (within their respective category). <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6622/throne-of-thunder">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Throne of Thunder</span></a> adds 3 new relevant passive trinkets and one lackluster active trinket, so as with Phase 1 &amp; 2 two passive trinkets are BiS. <br/>
<br/>
<ins>Passive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96561/lightning-imbued-chalice">
<img alt="Lightning-Imbued Chalice" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_mage_runeofpower.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightning-Imbued Chalice</span></a> is the strongest overall trinket of Phase 3, though it can be someone tricky to intentionally play around. Somewhat more reliable with the <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=114163/eternal-flame">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_torch_thrown.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Eternal Flame</span></a> build as it can proc of HoT effects; tracking the buff stacks can be beneficial for managing when the heal happens but in practice this should largely be unnecessary as the effect is a smart heal.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96385/horridons-last-gasp">
<img alt="Horridon's Last Gasp" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_eyeofthestorm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Horridon's Last Gasp</span></a> is a strong mana regeneration trinket, working similar to the BiS trinkets of the previous phases. Most of the time there is always more healing that can be done with extra mana (instead of using having to stop casting and melee for mana), but for exceedingly short encounters it is possible that this trinket can become superfluous, though the Intellect remains strong, particularly considering the alternative options lack this main stat.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96456/inscribed-bag-of-hydra-spawn">
<img alt="Inscribed Bag of Hydra-Spawn" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_creature_poison_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscribed Bag of Hydra-Spawn</span></a> is the closest to what can be considered an output trinket in Throne of Thunder, though having Spirit instead of Intellect, even when reforged, makes this trinket stumble in this role. While it is better than the options listed below, this trinket is not particularly appealing due to the unreliability of the effect and the relatively low proc rate; it can be somewhat challenging to have the shield effect occur on a specific desired target and not be wasted.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87163/spirits-of-the-sun">
<img alt="Spirits of the Sun" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_drink_29_sunkissedwine.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spirits of the Sun</span></a> was far and away the best trinket available in Phase One, and remains strong now though it falls behind somewhat due to iLvl differences. As a mana regen proc, there is largely no need to play around it in any particular way and it can simply be equipped and enjoyed.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86805/qin-xis-polarizing-seal">
<img alt="Qin-xi's Polarizing Seal" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_trinketpanda_10.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Qin-xi's Polarizing Seal</span></a> seems very similar to the highly valued Spirit proc trinkets at first glance, merely just reversed; in reality however it is slightly worse as Holy Paladin has few methods to take advantage of Intellect procs, while Spirit procs are always valuable (provided one is not at full mana). Fortunately the long duration and short internal cooldown of this trinket means it should be active very frequently.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79330/relic-of-chi-ji">
<img alt="Relic of Chi-Ji" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_crane.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Chi-Ji</span></a> is the Healer Darkmoon Deck of the expansion, and as is typical it is quite strong. Like Spirts of the Sun, Relic of Chi-Ji is very simple to use.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75274/zen-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Zen Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_scorchedstone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Alchemist Stone</span></a> while only available to Alchemists, Mists of Pandaria's version of this profession trinket can be very powerful when used to its full potential.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81133/empty-fruit-barrel">
<img alt="Empty Fruit Barrel" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cask_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Empty Fruit Barrel</span></a> is largely identical to Qin-xi's Polarizing Seal, but much weaker than the alternative options available.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81266/price-of-progress">
<img alt="Price of Progress" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_18.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Price of Progress</span></a>, while working slightly differently than the Spirit proc trinkets, is functionally the same.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Active Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="last">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94509/soothing-talisman-of-the-shado-pan-assault">
<img alt="Soothing Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_elemental_primal_life.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soothing Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault</span></a> is the new "mana-potion" trinket of Phase 3, which if equipped should be used on cooldown whenever not at maximum mana. The one drawback of this trinket is that as a non-raid item it is not available at an item-level where it can compete with the passive Heroic options, but it is otherwise quite strong and an upgrade over any previous phase trinkets.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96507/stolen-relic-of-zuldazar">
<img alt="Stolen Relic of Zuldazar" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_twilightfireward.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Stolen Relic of Zuldazar</span></a> is a decently strong trinket though the Spirit it gives is often largely irrelevant. The shield can be useful, particularly as it can be specifically target unlike the passive Inscribed Bag of Hydra-Spawn, but it is too weak to really make up for the lack of Intellect given by other Trinkets.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=93255/cutstitcher-medallion">
<img alt="Cutstitcher Medallion" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_spellcloththread.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cutstitcher Medallion</span></a> was the previous mana-potion effect trinket of Phase 2; at this point in the expansion there is very little if any reason to consider this trinket, especially as it is rep-gated.<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89080/scroll-of-revered-ancestors">
<img alt="Scroll of Revered Ancestors" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_archaeology_highborne_scroll.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Scroll of Revered Ancestors</span></a> is a strictly inferior, and also rep gated, version of Cutstitcher Medallion.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89081/blossom-of-pure-snow">
<img alt="Blossom of Pure Snow" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_herbd.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blossom of Pure Snow</span></a> was the strongest throughput Healing active trinket available in Phase One, but in Phase 3 it drawbacks are simply to large to ignore in the face of other far superior trinkets.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81264/vial-of-ichorous-blood">
<img alt="Vial of Ichorous Blood" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_08.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vial of Ichorous Blood</span></a> is a similar but weaker variant of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89080/scroll-of-revered-ancestors">
<img alt="Scroll of Revered Ancestors" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_archaeology_highborne_scroll.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Scroll of Revered Ancestors</span></a> used in the same manner.</div></li>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="reputation">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/achievement_faction_shadopan_assault.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reputation for Holy Paladins in Phase 3</span></h2>Phase 3 adds two new reputations, as well as a large amount of Celestial gear that essentially makes all Phase 1 &amp; 2 reputations relatively obsolete - though on the plus side Phase 2 items have been discounted by 25%, and Phase 1 items by 50%. <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/faction=1435/shado-pan-assault">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Shado-Pan Assault</span></a>, whose reputation is primarily (but not exclusively) gained through raiding <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6622/throne-of-thunder">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Throne of Thunder</span></a> gives access to many excellent items, though none that compete at the level of Heroic  gear. <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/faction=1387/kirin-tor-offensive">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Kirin Tor Offensive</span></a> /<wbr/> <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/faction=1388/sunreaver-onslaught">
