<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Holy Paladin</span></h2>With the Mists of Pandaria the new <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=112859/holy-insight">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_spiritualguidence.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Holy Insight</span></a> passive has been introduced, granting a 100% Hit chance on <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=20473/holy-shock">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_searinglight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Holy Shock</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=20271/judgment">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_righteousfury.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Judgment</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=35395/crusader-strike">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_crusaderstrike.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Crusader Strike</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=2812/denounce">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_purifyingpower.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Denounce</span></a>, which constitutes the entirety of the Holy Paladin's relevant ability to do damage, as well as functionally 100% Hit and Expertise on melee attacks through Spirit conversion in nearly all situations. Pieces with these stats can be used if there is absolutely no alternative available, but there is essentially zero reason to ever worry about pursuing Hit or Expertise cap on Holy Paladin in Mists of Pandaria, and healer pieces will always outperform any precision gear.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Holy Paladins</span></h2>Gems in Mists of Pandaria give twice as much secondary stats as they do main stat, meaning that there is an ideal option available for each slot color. The new Legendary quest item in Phase 3 is a Legendary Meta Gem, which should always be equipped once available. In general, the only variation between the <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=85804/selfless-healer">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_gaurdedbythelight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Selfless Healer</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=114163/eternal-flame">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_torch_thrown.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Eternal Flame</span></a> playstyles when gemming is that those playing Eternal Flame may want to make use of <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76699/quick-suns-radiance">
<img alt="Quick Sun's Radiance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_yellow.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Quick Sun's Radiance</span></a> in yellow or prismatic slots to reach a particular Haste Cap. See the Stat Priority guide for more information on this subject.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<ul class="exclude-units">
