<img alt="Sparkling Tinker's Gear" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sparkling Tinker's Gear</span></a></div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafting-professions">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/achievement_faction_craftsman.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Professions &amp; Crafted Gear for Holy Paladins</span></h2>In a similar fashion to racials an other aspects of character differentiation, in Mists of Pandaria most professions are all relatively close together, though as always gathering professions, (with the debatable exception of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=182/herbalism">
<img alt="Herbalism" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_herbalism.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Herbalism</span></a>), do fall significantly behind. Like Cataclysm, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=202/engineering">
<img alt="Engineering" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Engineering</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=165/leatherworking">
<img alt="Leatherworking" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_leatherworking.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leatherworking</span></a> are the default choices due to their movement speed boosts.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="engineering">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_engineering.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Engineering for Holy Paladins</h4>The perennial recommended profession for all classes, Engineering continues to be a powerful profession due to its access to <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55016/nitro-boosts">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nitro Boosts</span></a>. On average <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126731/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a> is equal to the stat gains of other professions, but being an active it allows the user to combine it with other cooldowns to multiply its benefit, (while also running the risk of the opposite happening due to misplay). If this wasn't enough, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77538/specialized-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Specialized Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Specialized Retinal Armor</span></a> is a Epic pre-raid option only available to engineers.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="leatherworking">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_leatherworking.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Leatherworking for Holy Paladins</h4>Leatherworking gives the standard profession boost of 320 Intellect via <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=124552/fur-lining-intellect">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_pelt_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fur Lining - Intellect</span></a>. Similar to Engineering its true value lies in access to extra items, in this case the notorious <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=185851/greater-drums-of-speed">
<img alt="Greater Drums of Speed" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_drum_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Greater Drums of Speed</span></a>.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="tailoring">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_tailoring.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Tailoring for Holy Paladins</h4>Tailoring is an interesting choice for Holy Paladins. While like Leatherworking the gear itself isn't useful, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=125481/lightweave-embroidery">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_thread_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightweave Embroidery</span></a> is a powerful proc that like Synapse Springs can be used to great effect with intelligent play. The downside is that the proc is much harder to play around than an on-demand active, and while its activation is predictable it is not preventable, opening up the potential for it to be completely wasted. Furthermore, Tailoring does not have an immediate second benefit as Engineering and Leatherworking do.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
