<del></del></span> Best Crafted Gear for Holy Paladins</span></h3>For the most part, crafted items are no longer restricted by profession, meaning that even if you aren't a Blacksmith, you can equip anything Blacksmiths craft. While not the best choice for any slot, and likely expensive at the beginning of the Phase, visiting the auction house can mean an easy power boost while waiting for loot to drop in raid. It is worth keep in mind however that any crafted item will be used for an exceedingly short amount of time, and the alternative options are relatively easy to acquire. If you do have excess gold the following items are worth some consideration and are all strong, particularly before new Celestial gear is available:<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94264/haunted-steel-headcover">
<img alt="Haunted Steel Headcover" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_plate_raidpaladin_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haunted Steel Headcover</span></a> is a Blacksmithing BoE piece that requires raid mats, and is thus likely to be relatively expensive. Considering this is a tier slot most should overlook this option, though it is decently strong in a vacuum.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94263/haunted-steel-greaves">
<img alt="Haunted Steel Greaves" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boot_plate_raidpaladin_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haunted Steel Greaves</span></a> is the other relevant Blacksmithing BoE added in Phase 3; while not a tier slot the lackluster stats here means this item has little use for Holy Paladins, except for perhaps quickly gearing up an alt character.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79330/relic-of-chi-ji">
<img alt="Relic of Chi-Ji" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_crane.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Chi-Ji</span></a> is the expansion's Darkmoon Deck for healers,<a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79325/crane-deck"> created by gathering cards from Inscription</a>, and remains a strong option in Phase 3, if outshined by the multiple new higher iLvl trinkets available.</div></li></ul>
